, "Ratings consensus is Tossup, with one rater at Tilt R"], "rationale": "Polling averages sit right at even and raters call it a Tossup, but all three prediction markets price Ford near 80%, and the freshest surveys show him narrowly ahead. That combination justifies a modest Democratic edge, tempered by Lombardo's incumbency in a purple state.", "watch": "Any late independent or Republican-sponsored polling showing Lombardo back ahead, or a shift in market pricing, would move this back toward Tossup.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["Incumbent Joe Lombardo (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Nevada's governor's race pits incumbent Republican Joe Lombardo against Democrat Aaron Ford in one of the closest contests of 2026. The state leans nearly even, and most recent polls show a margin within a few points either way, with the latest surveys giving Ford a small lead. Expert raters overwhelmingly call the race a Tossup, with one rating it Tilt Republican.\n\nThe sharpest divergence is with prediction markets, which price Ford's chances near 80 percent, well above what the polling alone would suggest. A third-party independent, Danielle Ford, is on the ballot and could siphon votes, and headlines highlight cross-currents including a teachers union endorsing Lombardo and anti-Trump sentiment in the state. The race remains genuinely competitive, with a slight Democratic tilt in the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4762, "margin": -0.32}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.447, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4885, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4837, "margin": -0.4}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -0.7}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4243, "margin": -0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4798, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4823, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4769, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4774, "margin": -0.5}, {"d